    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d601">

                <pb facs="0497" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg485"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/7044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé at Tangier</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Childs</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-29T23:00:00-04:00">October 29,
                            1942—11 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>203. Your 521, October 26. Note has been taken of the Spanish Government’s
                    decision. The approach suggested will be given careful consideration by the
                    Department.</p>
                <p>You may inform General Orgaz that his sympathetic interest in our proposal has
                    been warmly appreciated. At the same time you may also inform him that in
                    anticipation of the successful conclusion of the economic accord we had been
                    giving favorable consideration to <pb facs="0498" n="486" xml:id="pg486"/> the
                    matter of export licenses for important quantities of goods for Spanish Morocco,
                    and that in keeping with the General’s expressed interest in maintaining the
                    economy of Spanish Morocco the Department will endeavor to correlate the needs
                    of that area with the larger Spanish supply program.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
